{"about_the_game":"Originally released in 1983 for the ZX Spectrum, Terror-Daktil 4D gave players a unique twist on the traditional arcade shooter, as they must carefully aim arcing shots at flocks of enemies. The game also contains an opening cinematic cutscene - a rarity for early 80s computer games. Now, relive those days in this remastered emulated version.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\">Gameplay</h2>Survive for six days and six nights by firing arcing shots from your cannon at the fearsome Terror-Daktils.<br><br><br>This enhanced version introduces a number of modern features to this retro classic, including:<br><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li> Saving/loading the game at any point<br></li><li> Support for most modern game controllers<br></li><li> Full control remapping<br></li><li> Image scaling and smoothing options</li></ul>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/2005020?t=1654847096","background_raw":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/2005020?t=1654847096","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2005020/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1654847096","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2005020/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1654847096","categories":[{"description":"Single-player","id":2},{"description":"Partial Controller Support","id":18},{"description":"Steam Cloud","id":23},{"description":"Family Sharing","id":62}],"content_descriptors":{"ids":[],"notes":null},"detailed_description":"Originally released in 1983 for the ZX Spectrum, Terror-Daktil 4D gave players a unique twist on the traditional arcade shooter, as they must carefully aim arcing shots at flocks of enemies. The game also contains an opening cinematic cutscene - a rarity for early 80s computer games. Now, relive those days in this remastered emulated version.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\">Gameplay</h2>Survive for six days and six nights by firing arcing shots from your can